@@ -303,8 +303,9 @@ Note: New panels added or modified mostly not mentioned here for concision. See
 - **Search Bar**: shared by several Sevopedia pages; it allows to **search** for entries using the **keyboard**. The code is in [SevoPediaMain.py](/Assets/Python/Contrib/Sevopedia/SevoPediaMain.py). See [Sevopedia_reworks: search bar](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-01-added-a-search-bar-used-in-several-sevopedia-pages).
 - **Keyboard Navigation**: allows to **browse Sevopedia categories** using the keyboard in the list pages (e.g. In the Units Category: Axeman, Swordsman, Worker) or tree pages (e.g. Units Tree and Promotion Tree categories) using the **keyboard UP/DOWN arrow keys**. The code is in [SevoPediaMain.py](/Assets/Python/Contrib/Sevopedia/SevoPediaMain.py). See [Sevopedia_reworks: keyboard (UP/DOWN) navigation](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-02-added-keyboard-arrow-updown-navigation-support-used-in-several-sevopedia-pages).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5678+) **Fix empty pages** in Sevopedia **category opening flow:** opening a category now jumps **directly to the first real entry (if any)** instead of landing on a **blank header/spacer** row first; this makes **navigation easier** and avoids **needless and disruptive BACK/NEXT history pollution**. See [KI#119](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#119---fixed-sevopedia-category-opening-on-blank-placeholder-rows-item--1-and-polluting-backnext-history).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5729+) **Fix BACK/NEXT navigation history being lost on sevopedia exit** (e.g., to revisit AI Personality Panel pages during a game, or other categories previously visited): now **persists** during the entire **gaming session**. Added a **CLEAR** button to clear history. See [KI#125](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#125---fixed-base-advciv-issue-sevopedia-backnext-history-is-lost-on-exit).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5731+) Make **BACK**, **NEXT**, and **CLEAR** **greyed** when they have **no effect** (e.g., clicking NEXT when current page is already last visited, or BACK on first page visited since last clear). This was especially confusing before the navigation history persistence fix, when after reopening sevopedia after last sevopedia exit, BACK and NEXT button would be there but produce no effect at all (previous history was lost) (buttons are greyed now making such absence of effect clear). Note: Legend link is not greyed but instead is hidden if a category has no legend link (if there is a legend it is always active, and if there is none is it never active, so no need for a grey button). See [KI#126](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#126---fixed-sevopedia-footer-navigation-controls-looked-active-even-when-they-had-no-effect).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5729+) **Fix BACK/NEXT navigation history being lost on sevopedia exit** (e.g., to revisit AI Personality Panel pages during a game, or other categories previously visited): now **persists** during the entire **gaming session**. Added a **CLEAR** link to clear history. See [KI#125](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#125---fixed-base-advciv-issue-sevopedia-backnext-history-is-lost-on-exit).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5731+) Make **BACK**, **NEXT**, and **CLEAR** links **greyed** when they have **no effect** (e.g., clicking NEXT when current page is already last visited, or BACK on first page visited since last clear). This was especially confusing before the navigation history persistence fix, when after reopening sevopedia after last sevopedia exit, BACK and NEXT links would be there but produce no effect at all (previous history was lost) (links are greyed now making such absence of effect clear). Note: Legend link is not greyed but instead is hidden if a category has no legend link (if there is a legend it is always active, and if there is none is it never active, so no need for a grey link). See [KI#126](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#126---fixed-sevopedia-footer-navigation-controls-looked-active-even-when-they-had-no-effect).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5732+) New **Current-Game Player Id Previous/Next** links in **Sevopedia Leader** and **Sevopedia Civilization**: show `[-1` (previous) and `-1]` (next) greyed in the main menu/no **active game**. In game, they show nearby **known living** major-**player ids** for the **active player**, including the active player, without spoilers except in debug mode. Links are greyed when inactive. Example: if player ids are 0 to 10 and the active player is id 0 and knows ids 1, 4, and 9, possible links are `[-1` greyed / `0]` white from a leader/civ not in the current game list, `[0` greyed / `1]` white at id 0, `[0` white / `4]` white at id 1, `[1` white / `9]` white at id 4, and `[4` white / `9]` greyed at id 9. Corresponding **legend** sections added. Note: in custom games with duplicate leaders/civilizations, each duplicate leader/civilization appears once, using the first matching player id. Note 2: player id information is also available in the Info Screen's Score tab.
 - **Entries Grouping**: Depending on the Sevopedia Page, Sevopedia lists are now grouped: **by Civic Type** (e.g. Government, Economy) in Sevopedia Civics; **by Era Type** (e.g. Ancient Era, Classical Era, No Tech Prerequisite (available at any era)); **by Specialist Type** (e.g. Engineer vs Great Engineer) in Sevopedia Specialist; **by Improvement Type** (e.g. Farm -> Wheat/Maize, Pasture -> Sheep/Pig) in Sevopedia Bonus; **by Land/Water** (e.g. Land Improvements -> Farm/Pasture, Water Improvements -> Fishing Boats/Offshore Platform) sometimes with additional subgroups. Code implemented in [SevoPediaMain.py](/Assets/Python/Contrib/Sevopedia/SevoPediaMain.py) and [_sevopedia_main_groupings.py](/Assets/Python/Contrib/Sevopedia/_sevopedia_main_groupings.py).
 - the **Default First Sevopedia category opened** is changed from hardcoded Sevopedia Techs no matter its position to now **whichever category is the first in the category order**. Change in [SevoPediaMain.py](/Assets/Python/Contrib/Sevopedia/SevoPediaMain.py).
 - **Sevopedia Index** is now moved from the Tabs (bottom) to **its own category** for easier access and navigation between categories. Also implements the Search Bar.

